//
// The SAFETY EDGE the fix must not break (@P393).  `trim_start`/`trim_end` are
// declared `-> text[self]` — a BORROWED view of `self`, not a fresh owned store.
// Its return dep is NON-empty (`[self]`), so it must NEVER be freed at the call
// site: freeing it would release a slice of the caller's still-live `self` →
// use-after-free / double-free.
//
// Today these are clean inline-unbound (no free is emitted, correctly).  The fix
// for the de-NRVO'd OWNED case (01/03/05) keys on `dep.is_empty()` — owned
// returns have empty dep and get a free; borrowed `[self]` / NRVO'd `["??"]`
// returns have non-empty dep and are correctly skipped.  This probe is the
// regression guard that the guard stays correct.
//
// Expected:  interp = clean   native = clean   (and must remain clean post-fix)

fn main() {
  a = len("   hi".trim_start());   // borrowed text view, inline-unbound → no free
  b = len("hi   ".trim_end());     // borrowed text view, inline-unbound → no free
  println("a={a} b={b}");
}
